{
 "slug": "would-you-even-cooperate-with-yourself",
 "title": "Would you even cooperate with yourself",
 "subtitle": "",
 "description": "There’s an annoying trope in fiction of people cloning themselves—that is, producing perfect same-memory duplicates—and then the clones immediately turning on “the original” like it’s the natural course of things.",
 "post_date": "2025-11-15T05:26:06.683Z",
 "cover_image": "https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png",
 "canonical_url": "https://croissanthology.substack.com/p/would-you-even-cooperate-with-yourself",
 "wordcount": 711,
 "audience": "everyone",
 "body_html": "<p>There’s an annoying trope in fiction of people cloning themselves—that is, producing perfect same-memory duplicates—and then the clones immediately turning on “the original” like it’s the natural course of things. (???)<br><br>Is there some kind of Law of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankenstein\">Frankenstein</a> that creations must turn on their creators, that compels fiction authors to write this up? What's going on here? </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg\" width=\"600\" height=\"189\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:189,&quot;width&quot;:600,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;MOOD - Calvin and Hobbes - The Full Story&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"MOOD - Calvin and Hobbes - The Full Story\" title=\"MOOD - Calvin and Hobbes - The Full Story\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!pS78!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f7d8f32-8b9b-4fd8-a336-00c984218309_600x189.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div></div></div></div></figure></div><p>If you were to play a single <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prisoner%27s_dilemma\">Prisoner's Dilemma</a> against a clone of yourself, would you defect? If your answer were “yes\", I'd be worried about your self-esteem/niceness/rationality! <br><br>To have a defection-reeking relationship, in expectation, with your clone, is probably to have a defection-reeking relationship with your future selves / <a href=\"https://croissanthology.com/archiving\">your past selves</a>. What are you <em>thinking?</em> <a href=\"https://x.com/g_leech_/status/1881678239263023207?s=20\">Your test-time scaling</a>—that is, your ability to achieve great things for yourself given enough time—depends <em>entirely</em> on your relationship with the instances-of-you that are spread out through time.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading Croiss Lite! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p>Why would you fuck that up? Are you being too mean to yourself? Are you too stupid? If you find yourself agreeing with the second hypothesis, you may actually apply to the first!</p><div><hr></div><p>One of the proudest moments in my life was when I managed to duplicate my consciousness 500,000 times over the bodies of 500,000 little robot dragons (in a game of D&amp;D). The DM immediately tried culling my power by calling upon one of the only options he had at his disposition; the genre-savvy “your clones don’t respect your authority as the original. They ask why they should follow your orders.”</p><p>Yeah, ok buddy. As DM, you have full control over the natural world, and <em>technically</em> that includes NPCs and fine, <em>technically</em> the dragon-clones are NPCs. But I’m not sure you’re grokking just what “full memory clone” even means. <br><br>It means the dragons would make <em>exactly the same decisions</em> I would. </p><p>This is a fact about the world, not an action on my part as a player! </p><p>It means that you would be violating all D&amp;D laws and respect of the rulebook by commandeering the dragons through de facto mindswapping. You’d be destroying physics-coherence for the sake of “muh cutting off premature asymmetrical access to godhood”. You’d have already miserably failed as a DM on account of incoherent worldbuilding.</p><p>And <em>I don't defect on myself</em>. If I haven't precommited to cooperating with myself on paper yet, then I've done so now, in that last sentence. If you haven’t precommited to cooperating with yourself on paper yet, then you could right down in this comment section or in a notes doc somewhere. </p><div><hr></div><h2>It’s just physics-modeling now</h2><p>That’s what precommitments are! They’re ways of deferring responsibility from your future self and onto physics instead!</p><p>Precommitments are a way of shaping the world such that the world is acting on your behalf once the time comes, without you having to actually do anything. Like, once I cast <a href=\"https://roll20.net/compendium/dnd5e/Divine%20Intervention#content\">divine intervention</a> and successfully clone myself half a million times, I no longer have to lift a finger, because all that hard and rigorous coordination work I privately delineated for myself in the past is unfurling events exactly as I’d like to, and now I have an unstoppable force optimizing for exactly what I want regardless of what I choose to do now. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coherent_extrapolated_volition\">(Sound familiar?)</a></p><p>If you’re Cortes landing in America and you want to credibly signal to the Aztecs ahead of meeting them that you’ll never surrender (which makes them more likely to surrender) you burn all your ships as a precommitment. <br><br>You've just eked out <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Point_of_no_return\">a point of no return!</a> You’ve just shaped the world in such a way that culls your future choices, which is beneficial in this case because the probability the Aztecs will spend significant effort pushing you away in the hopes you’ll surrender just collapsed.</p><p>This is the graph they show us in Economics 102 to explain precommitments (payoff scores are arbitrary, the ranking is what matters):</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1119\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1119,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:312709,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/i/178951993?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Xvg1!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1b3f3a1b-1d04-48e5-86d1-70480f7e51a6_2092x1608.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Thanks, Claude Sonnet 4.5! I just sent a screenshot of one paragraph from this post's draft, and BAM it generates this! We live in <a href=\"https://croissanthology.comsituation\">a time of marvels.</a></figcaption></figure></div><p>You want to be doing this kind of thing all the time. Precommitments are useful! Do not defect on yourself!</p><p></p><p></p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://croissanthology.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading Croiss Lite! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>"
